A compiler

The `Compiler` holds the `Lexer`, the `Parser`, the `Checker` and the
`Code generator`. `Source` goes to the `Lexer`. The `Lexer` gives the `Parser`
the label `tokens`. The `Parser` gives the `Checker` the label `tree`. The
`Checker` gives the `Code generator` the label `tree`. The `Code generator`
writes the `Binary`, with the label `write`.
---
Compiler { Lexer, Parser, Checker, Code generator }
Source -> Lexer
Lexer -> Parser: tokens
Parser -> Checker: tree
Checker -> Code generator: tree
Code generator -> Binary: write
